{
  "info": {
    "name": "Fortinet FS-124F Standalone Monitoring",
    "description": "Monitoring/read-only API surface for standalone FortiSwitch FS-124F (FortiSwitchOS) sites, feeding a centralised custom dashboard.\n\n## Authentication \u2014 pick ONE of two modes\n\n**A) API token (FortiSwitchOS 7.x REST API admin \u2014 preferred).** Set the `api_token` variable in your environment. The collection-level auth sends `Authorization: Bearer {{api_token}}` on every request. Skip the `0 \u00b7 Auth \u2014 Session login` folder entirely.\n\n**B) Session login (works on all builds).** If your build has no REST API admin: set collection auth to `No Auth`, set `username`/`password` in the environment, run `Login (POST /logincheck)` once \u2014 Postman stores the APSCOOKIE session cookie automatically and the `ccsrftoken` value is saved to the `csrf_token` variable (needed only for write requests via the `X-CSRFTOKEN` header). Run `Logout` when finished; FortiSwitch limits concurrent admin sessions.\n\n## TLS\nSwitches ship with self-signed certs. For lab use disable 'SSL certificate verification' in Postman settings (File \u2192 Settings \u2192 General), or add the device cert under Settings \u2192 Certificates for production hygiene.\n\n## Conventions\nAll monitor endpoints are GET and safe to poll. Typical response envelope: `{\"http_method\":\"GET\",\"results\":[...],\"status\":\"success\",\"serial\":\"S124F...\",\"version\":\"v7.x.x\"}`. Port-scoped monitors accept `?port-name=portN`. Exact endpoint availability varies slightly per FortiSwitchOS train.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{api_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://192.0.2.10",
      "description": "Switch mgmt IP/FQDN, no trailing slash"
    },
    {
      "key": "api_token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "REST API admin token (auth mode A)"
    },
    {
      "key": "username",
      "value": "api-ro",
      "description": "Read-only admin (auth mode B)"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Password for auth mode B"
    },
    {
      "key": "csrf_token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Auto-filled by the Login request"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 \u00b7 Auth \u2014 Session login (only if no API token)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (POST /logincheck)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('login returned 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const jar = pm.cookies;",
                  "const csrf = jar.toObject ? jar.toObject()['ccsrftoken'] : undefined;",
                  "let token = csrf || (pm.cookies.get && pm.cookies.get('ccsrftoken'));",
                  "if (token) {",
                  "    token = token.replace(/\\\"/g, '');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('csrf_token', token);",
                  "    console.log('csrf_token saved for X-CSRFTOKEN header (writes only)');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.warn('ccsrftoken cookie not visible to script \u2014 GETs still work via session cookie; for writes copy it manually from the cookie jar');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{username}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "secretkey",
                  "value": "{{password}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "ajax",
                  "value": "1"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/logincheck",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "logincheck"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Form-encoded login. On success the device sets the APSCOOKIE_* session cookie (Postman keeps it automatically) and a ccsrftoken cookie. GET requests need only the session cookie; POST/PUT/DELETE also need header `X-CSRFTOKEN: {{csrf_token}}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout (POST /logout)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "End the admin session. FortiSwitchOS has a concurrent-session limit; poller code must always log out."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
